Has anyone else noticed that doors sometimes let you go through
them diagonally, and sometimes don't?  I find the seeming incon-
sistency here a bit bothersome, especially since the docs say
you can only go straight through.  (Is this all in my mind?)

I'd also like to lobby for a bit more natural behavior in cer-
tain types of animals.  After all, newts and geckos don't just
run up and attack.  Geckos will bite if startled, or if threat-
ened.  But I can't imagine them just wandering up and biting
someone.  Eh, maybe I'm being too picky.

I've recently gotten NetHack together here on a local Xenix
machine, and it's turned out to have a great side-benefit:  It
is teaching my 4 1/2 year-old to read pretty well.  He's asked
me a few questions, though, that I don't know enough (being a
rank amateur myself) to answer.  First is, "What do you use
fountains for, other than dipping & diluting things?"  Also,
"What good are things like potions that destroy armor?"  There
are a lot of potions that seem to do self-destructive things
if taken, and wizards naturally start out with lots of them.
I am curious myself:  Why would anyone want one of these po-
tions as is?

As I write this, my son asks also, "What do you do about heavy
iron balls?"  He also asks, "Why do they have lords?"  I've
wondered about this myself.  Is this simply a way of telling
us that a given monster is going to be tougher to kill than
usual?

-Richard


